# Line endings, pinned.  This repo is edited on Windows but its .sh files are shipped to a Linux box
# and its .py files run on both -- and a CRLF shell script fails on Linux with the classic
#     bash: $'\r': command not found
# which has already cost real debugging time in this project.  Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf)
# would happily introduce exactly that on checkout, so it is disabled in the repo AND pinned here.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.tsv  text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf
# binaries: never touch
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.pt binary
